  "summary": "Malicious code in prosodinetts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (131c62896875d39386abbfe87cb0ebfe46917a6c3e90f1dfb22464ea0a2b4626)\nThe package prosodinetts 0.1.0 contains no observed install-time or import-time code paths that read installer secrets, perform outbound network activity to attacker-controlled destinations, fetch and execute remote payloads, modify files outside the package's own directory, or establish persistence. No lifecycle hooks, dropper patterns, credential-harvest routines, or silent-relay mechanisms were identified in the shipped files.\n\n## Source: kam193 (8f39f72745f4cfbe04c6dd887e7fd8ac45dd9aef3e9892a41f6f7491997f901e)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
